WEBVTT

00:06.150 --> 00:08.520
Huh, Kanae, don't you have club work today?

00:09.010 --> 00:12.170
Sorry, I have to clean up at home today.

00:12.610 --> 00:14.670
Tell the president I'm
going to take the day off.

00:14.670 --> 00:16.090
Oh, yeah?

00:16.090 --> 00:18.100
Being a landlord is a lot of work, huh?

00:18.100 --> 00:21.410
Your birthday party the other
day was amazing, though.

00:22.070 --> 00:23.370
How did you do it?

00:27.480 --> 00:29.330
I don't really know.

00:29.330 --> 00:31.090
It must be hypnotism or something.

00:31.090 --> 00:33.300
Those people are so weird.

00:35.030 --> 00:37.200
Kanae! How's Motes-kun?

00:37.200 --> 00:39.050
He asked me out on a date.

00:39.290 --> 00:41.000
Can we go hang out again?

00:41.000 --> 00:42.100
Please!

00:42.100 --> 00:43.730
Well, like...

00:45.720 --> 00:46.900
See you later.

00:48.870 --> 00:51.350
Crap, crap, this is bad.

00:51.350 --> 00:54.110
I have to find some proper tenants soon.

00:54.110 --> 00:55.990
Tenants Wanted
Rooms Available
Terms Negotiable
Contact Otowa for Details
Otowakan

01:00.680 --> 01:04.300
You know, we musicians have
problems we can all relate to.

01:04.300 --> 01:05.370
I hate performing live.

01:05.370 --> 01:06.320
I know!

01:06.320 --> 01:08.320
I hate playing in front of other people.

01:08.320 --> 01:10.460
I got bummed out at dress rehearsal.

01:10.770 --> 01:12.560
It's been four days since
I bailed from the agency.

01:12.560 --> 01:13.840
Agency?

01:13.840 --> 01:14.970
What are you, professional?!

01:15.230 --> 01:17.550
All I've got going for
me right now is gaming.

01:17.550 --> 01:19.570
Wanna play again today?

01:19.570 --> 01:19.970
Okay.

01:20.570 --> 01:23.680
Well, then... Let's get started.

01:25.310 --> 01:27.780
Don't you have your own place?!

01:27.780 --> 01:31.490
Why are you using this room?
You don't even pay rent!

01:31.790 --> 01:34.110
The signal's good and your Internet's fast.

01:34.110 --> 01:37.380
I have no idea what you're talking about.

01:37.380 --> 01:39.200
Come on, it's vacant.

01:39.200 --> 01:42.030
The vacant rooms aren't for you.

01:42.440 --> 01:46.290
They're for my future tenants,
the ones who are going to pay rent.

01:46.750 --> 01:49.690
Someone might come for the open
house at the end of the week.

01:49.990 --> 01:53.500
I came home so I could start cleaning up.

01:53.500 --> 01:57.560
And yet here you are! Here you are!

01:57.560 --> 01:59.300
Oh, yeah. She was here.

01:59.300 --> 02:01.170
Your "future tenant."

02:01.170 --> 02:02.510
Maybe-ish?

02:02.510 --> 02:03.150
Huh?

02:03.150 --> 02:05.800
She said she wanted to
look inside the building.

02:05.800 --> 02:06.980
No way, where is she?

02:06.980 --> 02:08.260
I don't know.

02:08.260 --> 02:12.080
I saw her at the door, so I told them
to feel free to come check it out.

02:12.080 --> 02:14.020
You should have told me sooner!

03:45.870 --> 03:48.490
03: "Cho-chan and Lisz-chan"

03:52.790 --> 03:53.890
What's that noise?

03:56.070 --> 03:57.090
What's that noise?

04:02.270 --> 04:04.470
Round two!

04:13.920 --> 04:16.310
Please stop messing around
in the open rooms.

04:17.570 --> 04:19.290
Can I do it in your room?

04:18.750 --> 04:20.570
Enough already!

04:20.570 --> 04:22.210
I'm busy right now.

04:25.500 --> 04:27.460
What is wrong with this place?

04:27.460 --> 04:30.450
It's so run-down, and
something smells burnt.

04:31.000 --> 04:33.250
Are they really here?

04:42.500 --> 04:44.340
What is this place?

04:45.130 --> 04:46.980
It feels nostalgic.

04:48.520 --> 04:49.620
This room...

04:50.770 --> 04:51.900
This sensation...

04:53.110 --> 04:54.760
I feel like I'm going to remember something.

04:55.980 --> 04:57.050
Something...

04:59.440 --> 05:00.400
This...

05:02.540 --> 05:04.630
It's a mechanical organ.

05:06.980 --> 05:10.930
We held balls here, back in my grandma's day.

05:10.930 --> 05:13.860
This building actually has quite a history.

05:15.040 --> 05:16.710
Do you like it?

05:18.360 --> 05:21.280
There are five rooms available right now.

05:21.280 --> 05:23.800
We run a house share here.

05:23.800 --> 05:24.840
The kitchen is shared.

05:25.080 --> 05:26.340
The baths and washrooms are...

05:26.800 --> 05:28.600
Call me Lisz-chan.

05:29.430 --> 05:31.510
I'm Otowa Kanae, the landlord.

05:31.840 --> 05:33.890
My. You're the landlord?

05:34.300 --> 05:35.690
Yes.

05:35.690 --> 05:38.090
But you're still a student.

05:38.090 --> 05:39.900
How wonderful of you.

05:40.160 --> 05:42.500
What is this excitement that I'm feeling?

05:42.500 --> 05:44.320
This sense of nostalgia?

05:45.560 --> 05:46.750
What is this?

05:47.310 --> 05:48.460
Coming!

05:48.460 --> 05:50.270
I'm going to go get it.

05:51.600 --> 05:52.260
Oh.

05:53.480 --> 05:55.910
I have a delivery.

05:56.460 --> 05:57.410
What?

05:57.410 --> 06:00.410
203 is vacant.

06:00.410 --> 06:02.120
Chopping-san?

06:02.120 --> 06:03.390
Who's that?

06:03.760 --> 06:04.810
That's Cho-chan.

06:04.810 --> 06:06.360
Room 203, correct?

06:06.360 --> 06:07.240
Good.

06:07.240 --> 06:08.930
Who's that?

06:09.290 --> 06:10.330
H-Hey!

06:10.330 --> 06:11.410
Hey!

06:11.710 --> 06:13.680
Um... Sign, please.

06:18.710 --> 06:20.480
The seventh time's the charm.

06:21.720 --> 06:24.880
Behold, your trial of the day.

06:28.020 --> 06:30.610
Cho-chan, your package is here.

06:31.150 --> 06:32.310
Cho-chan.

06:32.610 --> 06:35.190
Like I said, that room is vacant.

06:35.190 --> 06:36.080
There's no one...

06:42.360 --> 06:44.670
Don-chan's in a good mood once again.

06:45.390 --> 06:46.800
Here I go, then!

06:51.040 --> 06:52.630
What's that noise?!

06:52.630 --> 06:53.930
Is someone in there?

06:54.270 --> 06:56.300
Did you invite yourself in?

06:56.300 --> 06:57.810
I'll call the cops—

06:57.810 --> 06:59.660
You can't scare him.

06:59.660 --> 07:01.580
Cho-chan's shy.

07:01.580 --> 07:04.010
Who the heck is Cho-chan?

07:04.010 --> 07:06.670
Don't make that face, my kitten.

07:06.670 --> 07:07.900
My kitten?!

07:08.830 --> 07:12.610
He must have gotten scared,
running away all the way here.

07:13.070 --> 07:14.770
I hope we can be good friends.

07:14.770 --> 07:15.330
What?!

07:15.590 --> 07:18.440
We're going to combine our
strengths to help Cho-chan out.

07:18.740 --> 07:20.390
Right...

07:32.090 --> 07:35.470
Gyoza is Firepower!!

07:35.720 --> 07:38.950
I'll have to exert my
authority as the landlord.

07:38.950 --> 07:40.300
I'm coming in.

07:40.610 --> 07:42.310
I already opened it.

07:42.610 --> 07:43.300
Huh?

07:43.810 --> 07:47.690
Potato Chips

07:44.270 --> 07:47.370
Isn't that the stuff they ordered?

07:46.230 --> 07:47.690
Cup Noodles

07:48.010 --> 07:51.670
Wait, they're totally set on living here!

07:51.970 --> 07:52.570
Oh.

07:52.570 --> 07:55.450
Live a Dazzling Life With These Secret Hints
<b>How to Make Money on the Internet!!</b>

07:52.880 --> 07:55.450
"Live a Dazzling Life With
These Secret Hints."

07:55.730 --> 07:58.450
"How to Make Money on the Internet!"?

08:00.050 --> 08:01.150
Don't look.

08:02.350 --> 08:03.670
Now, my kitten!

08:04.650 --> 08:05.170
Okay!

08:05.770 --> 08:07.460
Cho-chan, I'm here to pick you up.

08:07.460 --> 08:08.510
Coming in!

08:08.510 --> 08:09.550
Landl—

08:14.550 --> 08:16.480
Wh-What is this place?

08:17.190 --> 08:18.760
A recluse's room?

08:21.200 --> 08:24.840
Cho-chan, I know you're in here.

08:27.250 --> 08:29.310
Let's go back together.

08:31.260 --> 08:32.030
No.

08:32.970 --> 08:35.460
Why? I'm here for you.

08:35.460 --> 08:36.840
You're okay now, aren't you?

08:37.610 --> 08:38.370
No.

08:39.260 --> 08:40.520
I don't want to go home.

08:40.520 --> 08:41.500
Are you crazy?!

08:41.950 --> 08:43.860
Do you think you can live

08:43.860 --> 08:48.160
closed up in here?!

08:46.140 --> 08:48.170
Didn't you say not to scare him?!

08:48.690 --> 08:52.340
No, Wolf, living in the unopenable 203

08:52.340 --> 08:54.850
is the Gyoza Fairy, Gyozary.

08:55.200 --> 08:58.180
Over the past several days,
she has been attempting to

08:58.180 --> 08:59.890
communicate the essence of gyoza to me.

08:59.890 --> 09:01.430
No way.

09:01.430 --> 09:03.430
It's a lonely ghost.

09:03.430 --> 09:05.150
It likes it when you make

09:05.150 --> 09:07.810
a lot of noise, so let's call it Don-chan.

09:08.390 --> 09:09.020
Huh?

09:09.400 --> 09:11.530
Is it just me,

09:11.530 --> 09:13.530
or is 203 open?

09:13.530 --> 09:15.200
It may not just be you.

09:15.680 --> 09:16.950
Do you hear something?

09:16.950 --> 09:18.530
I may hear something.

09:18.790 --> 09:21.410
Cho-chan!

09:21.670 --> 09:23.290
Are you Don-chan?!

09:23.290 --> 09:24.290
Gyozary?!

09:31.360 --> 09:34.550
I've finally found you, Beethoven, Mozart.

09:37.500 --> 09:39.530
We're returning home.

09:39.530 --> 09:40.470
What?!

09:40.990 --> 09:41.790
What?

09:42.740 --> 09:46.220
Dude, Chopin-san, did you pass out?

09:46.980 --> 09:48.750
The gyoza tastes so weird...

09:48.750 --> 09:50.460
They keep banging on the floor...

09:50.460 --> 09:52.680
The landlord came in and stuff...

09:53.010 --> 09:54.990
I'm hiding in the closet.

09:55.960 --> 09:56.750
What?

09:56.750 --> 09:58.410
Stop it, please!

09:58.410 --> 10:00.300
Silence, Landlord!

10:00.600 --> 10:02.740
Do you love my gyoza that much?

10:03.050 --> 10:04.710
Do you envy it?!

10:04.710 --> 10:05.350
Ow!

10:05.350 --> 10:07.000
That hurt, Don-chan.

10:07.410 --> 10:08.460
Landlord?

10:08.760 --> 10:09.970
Gyoza?

10:09.970 --> 10:11.140
Don-chan?

10:12.380 --> 10:13.650
You're upstairs?!

10:18.010 --> 10:18.630
I'm hiding in the closet.

10:18.720 --> 10:21.010
So many scary people... Help me.

10:27.890 --> 10:29.340
You're not getting away now.

10:29.340 --> 10:32.020
Cho-chan got away while
I was looking for you two.

10:32.330 --> 10:33.900
I wasn't sure <i>what</i> I was going to do.

10:34.270 --> 10:35.300
Looking for us?

10:35.600 --> 10:36.240
Why?

10:36.680 --> 10:38.200
Because I get a lot of complaints.

10:38.460 --> 10:39.200
From who?

10:40.700 --> 10:44.330
Do you not remember the agency or anything?

10:44.330 --> 10:44.700
A...

10:44.700 --> 10:45.080
...gen...

10:45.080 --> 10:45.790
...cy?

10:46.670 --> 10:47.790
Stop fighting!

10:48.320 --> 10:51.620
I'll tell you about the agency.

10:53.020 --> 10:54.570
Who's this kid?

10:54.570 --> 10:55.420
I know, right?

10:55.420 --> 10:58.300
Come on, hear me out.

11:01.680 --> 11:03.350
So that's how it was, huh?

11:03.560 --> 11:06.860
Well, Chopin's shy.

11:06.860 --> 11:09.930
Mainstream live performances
are hard on him.

11:09.930 --> 11:12.030
He ran away because he didn't agree
with the agency's way of doing things.

11:12.030 --> 11:13.830
That happens all the time in the biz.

11:14.130 --> 11:16.170
I love live performances.

11:16.470 --> 11:19.860
I had no idea that's how Cho-chan felt.

11:20.160 --> 11:22.090
In other words,

11:22.090 --> 11:25.570
he doesn't like doing flashy performances
in front of other people.

11:25.570 --> 11:27.250
You're more cool

11:27.250 --> 11:29.710
working online these days.

11:29.710 --> 11:32.120
As a fellow musician,

11:32.120 --> 11:34.130
I totally know what that's like.

11:34.710 --> 11:37.470
Your musician appeal is getting annoying.

11:37.770 --> 11:40.010
How would you know about that?

11:40.330 --> 11:43.100
He's always on my server.

11:43.100 --> 11:46.640
So we started talking about our problems
and stuff as we were chatting.

11:46.950 --> 11:49.180
So he just happens to game with you.

11:49.400 --> 11:52.160
Seriously though, to think
he was actually a pro.

11:52.160 --> 11:53.710
Why is he here?

11:53.710 --> 11:56.120
When did he even get here?

11:57.360 --> 11:59.580
CryingDarkAngel?

12:00.250 --> 12:01.640
That's me, Chopin.

12:01.640 --> 12:03.500
CryingDarkAngel.

12:03.500 --> 12:05.820
Can you believe we were so close?

12:06.260 --> 12:09.590
Well, you had your location
info all over the place.

12:09.590 --> 12:12.200
I didn't have a place to go
after I left the agency, so...

12:12.200 --> 12:12.940
So I came here.

12:12.940 --> 12:15.660
Oh wow, so you came to find me!

12:15.660 --> 12:18.340
Isn't that what they talk about when
they say to be careful online?

12:18.840 --> 12:19.760
Here it is.

12:20.260 --> 12:22.760
The ultimate gyoza, this time.

12:23.280 --> 12:25.670
Now, consume it, my fairy!

12:25.670 --> 12:27.130
If you have to eat gross
food, you might as well

12:27.130 --> 12:29.430
have fun eating with a bunch
of people, right, Don-chan?

12:29.430 --> 12:30.760
Oh, yeah!

12:30.760 --> 12:32.270
Let's have a gyoza meetup, Chopin!

12:32.510 --> 12:33.520
Yes.

12:33.520 --> 12:36.750
Anything to get you to come out, Cho-chan.

12:36.750 --> 12:38.030
Cho-chan-san.

12:43.530 --> 12:44.790
It's delicious!

12:44.790 --> 12:46.020
Don-chan!

12:46.020 --> 12:48.700
This is so great.

12:49.140 --> 12:50.560
It's the best in the world!

12:55.290 --> 12:56.830
It smells good.

13:04.680 --> 13:06.610
They're having so much fun.

13:10.850 --> 13:11.680
Now!

13:19.320 --> 13:21.480
Oranges

13:21.940 --> 13:23.310
What is this?

13:23.610 --> 13:25.160
He's still scared.

13:25.160 --> 13:26.650
It's okay, Cho-chan.

13:26.650 --> 13:28.600
Let's speak of gyoza all night!

13:28.600 --> 13:31.250
Sweet hat! So square!

13:31.250 --> 13:32.330
I know, right?

13:32.330 --> 13:34.430
It's the worst when you
first start going big.

13:35.010 --> 13:36.210
Come on, Cho-chan!

13:35.010 --> 13:36.210
Come on, Fairy!

13:38.670 --> 13:42.220
Excuse me! Fill out the
tenancy form, please.

13:42.220 --> 13:43.420
Tenancy?

13:43.420 --> 13:45.370
He's coming home with me.

13:45.670 --> 13:47.980
I thought you wanted him out.

13:47.980 --> 13:51.210
He used a room without my consent,
and he made a huge mess.

13:51.580 --> 13:55.530
He needs to pay his deposit, his fees,
and his rent to make up for it.

13:55.530 --> 13:58.510
Or would you rather take responsibility?

13:58.510 --> 14:00.580
Oh, my.

14:00.580 --> 14:03.520
Your patronizing, your lecturing...

14:03.520 --> 14:04.780
It gives me chills!

14:05.080 --> 14:06.580
What is this?

14:05.870 --> 14:07.330
Are you even listening?

14:07.200 --> 14:08.970
More! More!

14:07.640 --> 14:09.540
Can I live here

14:10.370 --> 14:14.030
if I sign that?

14:14.570 --> 14:16.330
Welcome, Don-chan!

14:14.570 --> 14:16.330
Welcome, Fairy!

14:19.740 --> 14:23.500
I can't deal with people I don't know!

14:31.420 --> 14:36.380
Twoja muzyka obróci się w nicość.

14:38.890 --> 14:40.740
The past is a fantasy.

14:41.170 --> 14:43.170
The future is a blank canvas.

14:43.170 --> 14:45.190
Therefore I shall

14:46.000 --> 14:48.240
paint it with Musik.

14:49.290 --> 14:52.290
Reviving,

14:52.290 --> 14:56.000
Being reborn,

14:56.000 --> 15:02.630
Past wounds throbbing

15:02.630 --> 15:09.300
This foolish, frail human

15:04.850 --> 15:06.020
What's this?

15:06.550 --> 15:08.260
Nocturne No. 2.

15:08.730 --> 15:12.010
The most famous of

15:09.300 --> 15:15.550
Embraced by a flame in the darkness

15:12.010 --> 15:14.320
Frédéric Chopin's 21 Nocturnes.

15:14.660 --> 15:16.020
It's Musik.

15:15.550 --> 15:23.810
This trial of God

15:17.020 --> 15:18.810
Cho-chan's Musik?

15:19.570 --> 15:21.410
He remembered?

15:21.410 --> 15:23.810
Is it that weird hypnosis again?

15:23.810 --> 15:29.440
Is a cruel destiny

15:27.810 --> 15:28.280
Wait!

15:28.770 --> 15:29.960
Cho-chan-san!

15:29.740 --> 15:40.530
Guiding the wandering souls

15:30.280 --> 15:31.460
Wait, you!

15:32.780 --> 15:35.240
I finally have a tenant.

15:35.480 --> 15:38.750
You aren't getting away!

15:39.150 --> 15:41.750
How is that girl so powerful?

15:42.150 --> 15:44.010
Where does she get her power?

15:44.750 --> 15:46.000
Is this another...

15:46.810 --> 15:47.730
Is this...

15:48.320 --> 15:49.420
Is this...

15:50.310 --> 15:52.340
What is this?!

16:01.580 --> 16:02.770
It's warm.

16:11.880 --> 16:13.020
Yes.

16:13.860 --> 16:16.740
Yes, I remember, now.

16:17.510 --> 16:19.160
This, too...

16:20.210 --> 16:21.260
Is love!

16:24.710 --> 16:26.910
Musik ist liebe,

16:26.910 --> 16:30.880
liebe ist Musik!

16:45.510 --> 16:46.640
This sensation...

16:46.640 --> 16:48.090
I know now.

16:48.070 --> 16:53.540
Your eyes, trembling like a droplet

16:48.730 --> 16:50.630
Yes, love!

16:50.630 --> 16:52.200
It's love!

16:53.540 --> 16:58.130
A flower, blooming as if to sing

16:56.520 --> 16:57.900
What is this song?

16:58.430 --> 17:04.170
At the end of a dear wait

16:59.960 --> 17:02.050
Liebesträume No. 3.

17:02.350 --> 17:05.360
Franz List's signature piece, named,

17:04.170 --> 17:09.230
To be embraced by you

17:05.360 --> 17:07.600
"Love as Long as You Can."

17:08.170 --> 17:11.010
Ah, the pianist boy.

17:09.530 --> 17:14.860
Changing winds, wandering hills

17:11.470 --> 17:13.640
I met him at a performance, once.

17:13.640 --> 17:15.760
Boy?! He's a man?!

17:14.860 --> 17:21.770
Hesitation, too, becomes
strength to move forward

17:15.990 --> 17:18.340
Man, lucky guy.

17:18.340 --> 17:20.800
How come he gets those things? No fair.

17:20.800 --> 17:21.770
<i>That's</i> what gets you?

17:22.800 --> 17:30.840
Of music, make life, with clear love

17:23.860 --> 17:25.710
Cho-chan-san...

17:28.220 --> 17:28.980
Huh?

17:30.840 --> 17:38.910
Paint with vibrance an
arrow dreaming of love

17:32.940 --> 17:36.380
Don't!

17:38.910 --> 17:44.200
With the colors of the waves

17:44.200 --> 17:48.980
With purity, as if to tumble,

17:47.590 --> 17:48.730
It stopped.

17:48.980 --> 17:54.900
Sing with your slightly broken smile

17:51.940 --> 17:53.970
Where am I?

17:54.900 --> 17:59.800
So that you may be there where I touch

18:00.170 --> 18:05.550
The opening sky, the darkness of shame

18:05.550 --> 18:12.640
Set it aside, wavering is
the shadow of resignation

18:11.590 --> 18:13.530
Cho-chan-san.

18:13.530 --> 18:21.560
Forgive me for delivering my
rainbow-colored love to you

18:20.270 --> 18:21.870
Dear adorable landlord,

18:21.560 --> 18:30.520
Paint a dream of an arrow of
love, of the promised time

18:22.380 --> 18:25.720
give him all of your love.

18:31.900 --> 18:35.420
Welcome to my grandmother's mansion!

18:37.930 --> 18:39.050
More, more!

18:40.650 --> 18:45.500
Changing winds, wandering hills

18:42.670 --> 18:43.470
Really?

18:44.000 --> 18:45.500
I'm so shy, though.

18:45.500 --> 18:56.530
Hesitation, too, becomes
strength to move forward

18:46.150 --> 18:47.480
I'm so pasty.

18:49.010 --> 18:50.690
Love is forgiveness.

18:50.940 --> 18:51.880
It's okay.

18:51.880 --> 18:53.910
It's okay if you're pasty.

18:53.910 --> 18:55.690
It's okay if you're shy.

18:55.690 --> 18:58.060
It's okay if you don't pay rent.

18:57.480 --> 19:05.520
Of music, make life, with clear love

18:59.180 --> 19:00.860
So long as I get to live with you,

19:01.200 --> 19:03.470
I don't need anything else!

19:03.470 --> 19:05.520
Landlord-san!

19:05.520 --> 19:13.480
Paint with vibrance an
arrow dreaming of love

19:06.130 --> 19:07.580
I feel it!

19:07.880 --> 19:11.880
There's love in this mansion!

19:13.480 --> 19:21.560
My beautiful, rainbow-like love is forgiven

19:17.890 --> 19:18.800
What the what?!

19:21.560 --> 19:30.480
Paint with vibrancy an
arrow dreaming of love

19:24.430 --> 19:27.100
Don-chan!

19:24.430 --> 19:27.100
Fairy!

19:24.430 --> 19:27.100
Chopin!

19:28.020 --> 19:30.480
Being a musician is great.

19:31.020 --> 19:33.300
To gyoza and beyond!

19:33.740 --> 19:36.060
I'm waiting for your floor slam.

19:36.810 --> 19:37.780
Guys...

19:38.330 --> 19:40.370
Guys!

19:40.760 --> 19:42.700
Yes, all of us.

19:43.410 --> 19:46.340
That is love!

19:55.470 --> 19:57.760
D-Did I say something?

19:57.760 --> 19:59.470
About not paying rent or something?

20:02.120 --> 20:04.510
I can't stand strangers!

20:07.550 --> 20:08.250
What?

20:08.910 --> 20:12.030
So now he hates me?

20:24.520 --> 20:26.960
I seriously hope I find a proper tenant

20:26.960 --> 20:29.750
who's going to pay rent this time.

20:32.280 --> 20:34.290
Lisz-chan-san?

20:36.600 --> 20:38.330
You're still here?

20:38.330 --> 20:39.920
You don't need to use "-san."

20:40.220 --> 20:41.140
Here you go.

20:41.630 --> 20:44.260
Tenancy Agreement

20:42.080 --> 20:44.260
The tenancy agreement?

20:46.120 --> 20:47.430
It's done properly.

20:49.680 --> 20:51.900
Rent!

20:52.240 --> 20:54.130
For the first time in my life.

20:54.430 --> 20:56.310
Thank you, Landlord.

20:57.980 --> 21:00.800
Welcome to Otowakan.

21:08.540 --> 21:11.550
Speaking of which, I want a pet.

21:12.010 --> 21:13.610
Don-chan, you're still here?

21:13.610 --> 21:15.060
My fairy!

21:15.670 --> 21:17.670
Quiet Boy!!
I'm a Pet
Please Take Me

21:18.060 --> 21:20.560
My name is Frédéric Chopin.

21:20.900 --> 21:22.090
Nice to meet you.

21:22.400 --> 21:24.160
I'll have to raise your rent.

21:24.160 --> 21:24.910
For the pet.

21:25.210 --> 21:26.260
I thought so.

21:26.560 --> 21:27.590
He's not even a pet.

21:27.870 --> 21:30.230
You guys are living here, Lisz-chan?

21:30.230 --> 21:33.420
There're four of us ClassicaLoids
here now. That's hilarious.

21:33.420 --> 21:35.970
Class... say what?

21:35.970 --> 21:37.330
Lucky you.

21:37.330 --> 21:39.230
Why did you get to become a woman?

21:39.230 --> 21:41.260
"Get to become?" What?

21:41.260 --> 21:42.390
It must be fate.

21:42.390 --> 21:43.110
Huh?!

21:43.520 --> 21:44.900
I don't know.

21:45.330 --> 21:47.390
What does it matter?

21:49.420 --> 21:51.870
This is Matsuhama Realty speaking.

21:51.870 --> 21:54.370
I'm told you would be the guarantor

21:54.370 --> 21:56.230
to Liszt-san's apartment contract.

21:56.230 --> 21:58.240
Is this correct?

21:58.540 --> 22:00.630
This is just a confirmation.

22:00.630 --> 22:02.370
If there are no mistakes—

22:04.880 --> 22:08.820
Why does everyone who goes
there end up not coming back?

22:08.820 --> 22:11.310
It's just us now.

22:12.100 --> 22:12.770
Huh?

22:13.360 --> 22:15.120
Isn't someone missing?

22:15.420 --> 22:16.310
Yeah.

22:16.950 --> 22:18.240
Um...

22:18.540 --> 22:19.790
It's...

22:22.460 --> 22:23.970
Who was it again?

22:29.940 --> 22:31.610
Beethoven-senpai...

22:40.000 --> 22:43.000
To be continued

24:12.970 --> 24:27.820
04: "Wandering Kouhai"

24:13.320 --> 24:14.680
Wandering soul.

24:14.680 --> 24:16.010
Heart full of desire.

24:16.010 --> 24:18.250
A dried-up mind passes through time.

24:18.250 --> 24:20.570
Oh, where art thou, my supreme?

24:20.570 --> 24:22.190
From the starving soul comes a

24:22.190 --> 24:25.560
super, super, super, super relaxing Musik.

24:25.560 --> 24:28.860
The whole world chillaxes to the max
and turns all baby-like and stuff.
